    "head_branch": "feature/parting-pair-search",
    "head_commit_message": "perf(native): parting's pair search on the flat grid with a neighbour list (spec 41 step 3)\n\nThe pair search moves to parting/pairs.rs. Pairs are found through grid::Grid, not a hashed\nbucket map. Each chunk of bodies fills one buffer with each body's partners sorted, so there\nis no global sort and no per-body Vec. A neighbour list with a 0.25-cell skin is shared by a\ntick's passes and rebuilt when a body moves more than half the skin. Each pass applies\nUnitBodies._pairs' test in list order, so the pairs and their order are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011AyPi58viunhUkxUyZXV1T",
